> "Entrepreneurship isn't just about building enterprises. It's about building people."
>
> Serve Funding

## Michael's Memo: Wisdom From Estonia

We just returned from Tallinn, Estonia, a city that surprised me in many ways. We went to visit our son, who moved there recently. While we were there he got engaged to his Estonian fiancée. Amazing.

Looking back, I realized that beyond the special family milestone, I was inspired by the innovative, entrepreneurial spirit alive and well there. Estonia is one of the most business-friendly countries in the world. The clarity, the digital infrastructure, and the trust-based business culture all fuel innovation.

While there, I had the privilege of sitting down with four incredible Estonian entrepreneurs and getting to know them. These seasoned business owners are deeply invested in building and innovating, and that includes mentoring the next generation, our son among them.

Their wisdom, generosity, and example reminded me of a deep truth I believe in: entrepreneurship isn't just about building enterprises. It's about building people.

I returned from Tallinn extremely grateful. For the beauty of the city and the rich culture of Estonia. For the entrepreneurial spirit of our son, who is forging a life there. And for the privilege of learning from fellow innovators who are building up companies and the next generation.

Let's keep building: enterprises, people, and relationships that last.

Here to serve,

Michael Kodinsky, Founder & CEO

## Deal Highlight: $1.475MM Bridge to a Medical and Surgical Practice Sale

A successful surgeon running multiple medical and surgical practices in the Southeast was accepting an offer from a large hospital system to buy his companies. A liquidity event was pending, but he needed substantial short-term capital to bridge the gap, and fast.

His private banker at a major national bank referred him to her counterpart on the commercial team, a banker with a nine-year relationship with Michael. Together we determined the doctor needed to cover important year-end business expenses with more than $1.25MM inside a few short weeks.

Serve delivered multiple options, including an interest-only bridge loan tied to the doctor's property and several revenue-based business term loans. As usual, we negotiated aggressively on the client's behalf and secured the deal that best matched the company's required timing, cost of funds, and repayment structure.

**Results:**

- $1.475MM funded
- Flexible bridge structure with aggressive prepay discounts
- Delivered in under two weeks, well inside the client's tight timeframe

This deal didn't just solve for cash flow. It gave the founder peace of mind and protected his upside.

## More Than Money: The Power of Strategic Connections

One of the most valuable takeaways from my time in Estonia? The impact of proximity to other purpose-driven people.

Whether it's across the globe or at your next client lunch, every encounter has the potential to unlock insight, share wisdom, or forge opportunity. In this business, and in life, the right connections shape the journey.

That's why Serve Funding exists not just to fund companies, but to cultivate a trusted ecosystem of visionary entrepreneurs, bankers, and advisors.

Capital funds growth. Community fuels it. We're honored to walk alongside those who build both.
